  "rawCandidate": "```json\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"selectedContextPaths\":[\"README.md\",\"config/app.json\",\"src/greeting.py\",\"src/main.py\"],\"plan\":{\"mutationTargets\":[],\"requestedCheckIds\":[]},\"answer\":{\"kind\":\"read_only\",\"files\":[],\"citations\":[\"README.md\",\"config/app.json\",\"src/greeting.py\",\"src/main.py\"],\"findingIds\":[],\"summary\":\"The configured audience reaches stdout through a four-step chain. README.md establishes the entry point and configuration location: 'Configuration lives in `config/app.json`; execution begins in `src/main.py`.' The audience value itself is defined in config/app.json as the `audience` field (\\\"traveler\\\"). src/main.py is the entry point: it reads config/app.json, parses the JSON, extracts the `audience` key, passes it to `greeting()`, and wraps the result in `print(...)`, which writes to stdout. src/greeting.py provides the greeting behavior, returning the formatted string `f\\\"Welcome, {audience}.\\\"` for the passed audience. Thus: config/app.json supplies the audience -> src/main.py loads it and calls greeting -> src/greeting.py formats the welcome message -> print() emits it to stdout.\"}}\n```",
